preConditionHook:
// THE 3/10 OSCILLATOR -- Grimes's fast line, in the settled form (merge
// decision 2): the difference of two SIMPLE averages of the close,
//     osc = average of close over fastLen bars, less the average
//           of close over slowLen bars
// with fastLen 3 and slowLen 10 as the book's defaults. Never the MACD word.
// EL's Average RECOMPUTES from scratch every bar (VERIFIED: matched a fresh
// loop on 2,808/2,808 bars; it is NOT a rolling accumulator like the WFSafe_
// wrappers), and Summation adds the newest bar first and works backwards,
// with a single divide at the end -- which is how the loops below run.
// Both averages run over a PRICE expression, which has real bar history, so
// they are recomputed from the bars rather than mirrored; only osc ITSELF is
// a variable, and that is what the ring buffer below mirrors. Copied from
// OscillatorAboveZero and OscillatorNewExtreme, the family's reference pair.
// The whole quantity is a difference of prices, so it passes the shift test.
// Scratch is declared in localVariables, never at hook scope: the generator
// only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration is a
// redefinition when the rule is placed twice in one strategy.
oscFast = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)fastLen; ++i) {
    oscFast += close[i];
}
oscFast = oscFast / (int)fastLen;
oscSlow = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)slowLen; ++i) {
    oscSlow += close[i];
}
oscSlow = oscSlow / (int)slowLen;
osc = oscFast - oscSlow;
// THE FAST-LINE ARTIFACT WINDOW, Appendix B. For the first slowLen bars after
// a genuine trend inflection the fast line's curvature is an artifact of the
// slowLen-period average rolling into the new regime, not new momentum. The
// rule is true -- those reads are trustworthy -- once more than slowLen bars
// have passed since the anchor.
//
// THE ANCHOR is the OSCILLATOR ZERO CROSS, the C-list resolution of the
// merge's open question; decision 2 records that cross as MovingAverageCross
// at fastLen/slowLen. Either direction counts, so both sides are identical.
//
// THE WINDOW LENGTH IS slowLen AND IS NOT SEPARATELY TUNABLE: Appendix B's
// proof is that the distortion lasts exactly as long as the slow average takes
// to roll over.
//
// EL's crosses above/below is a VERIFIED STATE MACHINE (the `crosses` register
// row), not a two-bar test: a cross fires on a bar whose toleranced relation
// is above/below AND whose most recent NON-EQUAL relation was on the other
// side. An equality run is bridged and the state starts UNKNOWN, so nothing
// fires until a non-equal relation has been observed. Mirrored exactly as
// MovingAverageCross does, which is why osc[1] is never read: that would be
// the variable's zero-filled pre-history.
crossed = false;
if (el_gt(osc, 0.0)) {
    crossed = (lastSide == -1);
    lastSide = 1;
} else if (el_lt(osc, 0.0)) {
    crossed = (lastSide == 1);
    lastSide = -1;
}
// el_eq: equality run -- lastSide deliberately unchanged, no cross.
// Before any cross has been observed the counter counts bars since the
// strategy's first bar, so the rule reads true after slowLen bars: the
// permissive polarity a window blocker wants during warm-up, and the literal
// reading BarsSinceEmaCross gives the same counter.
if (crossed) {
    barsSinceInflection = 0;
} else {
    barsSinceInflection = barsSinceInflection + 1;
}
